---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Founder from '../../components/Founder.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../../components/CtaBlock.astro';
import JsonLd from '../../components/JsonLd.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, personSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
const person = personSchema();
import { site, isLive } from '../../data/site';
const team = site.founder.team;
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="CAVELDON is a founder-led cloud engineering practice focused on AWS, Azure, security, governance, reliability and sound technical decisions.">
  <JsonLd data={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]), ...(person ? [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', ...person }] : [])]} />
  <section class="page-hero gridpaper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>About</span></nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">About CAVELDON</p>
      <h1>Why CAVELDON exists.</h1>
      <p class="lead">CAVELDON is built around a simple belief: technology should create confidence, not unnecessary complexity. We focus on the architecture, security controls and operational foundations that modern software depends on.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="who-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Who you’ll work with</p><h2 id="who-title">Founder-led engineering.</h2></div>
        <p class="intro">The goal is clear technical responsibility, realistic scope and work a customer can understand and maintain. The founder’s experience informs the approach; any additional delivery roles should be introduced transparently.</p>
      </div>
      <Founder />
      {team.length > 0 && (
        <div class="cells cols-3 team-list">
          {team.map(m => <div><span class="cell-num">ENGINEER</span><h3 style="margin:10px 0 4px">{m.name}</h3><p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:16px">{m.role}</p>{m.linkedin && <a class="link" style="margin-top:10px" href={m.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a>}</div>)}
        </div>
      )}
      {team.length === 0 && !isLive && <p style="margin-top:24px"><span class="ph">[Team members appear here once hired: add them to founder.team in src/data/site.ts]</span></p>}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Experience &amp; evidence</p><h2 id="evidence-title">Clear labels for where experience comes from.</h2></div>
        <p class="intro">CAVELDON is a new practice. We distinguish work delivered by CAVELDON from experience gained in earlier employment and from independent Engineering Lab reference work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cells cols-3">
        <div><span class="cell-num">CAVELDON WORK</span><h3 style="margin:12px 0 8px">Client-authorized evidence</h3><p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:16px">Only engagements delivered through CAVELDON appear as CAVELDON client work, and only when the customer permits publication.</p></div>
        <div><span class="cell-num">PRIOR EXPERIENCE</span><h3 style="margin:12px 0 8px">Professional work before CAVELDON</h3><p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:16px">Relevant experience gained as an employee or contractor is described as prior professional experience, without implying it was delivered by CAVELDON or disclosing confidential information.</p></div>
        <div><span class="cell-num">ENGINEERING LAB</span><h3 style="margin:12px 0 8px">Reference designs and validation</h3><p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:16px">Lab studies show technical reasoning and planned validation. Each study states what has and has not been implemented or tested.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt" aria-labelledby="values-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">How we work</p><h2 id="values-title">Four promises we hold ourselves to.</h2></div>
        <p class="intro">The founding idea is simple: technology should create confidence, not complexity.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cells cols-4">
        <div><span class="cell-num">01 · CLARITY</span><h3 style="margin:12px 0 8px">Understand before changing</h3><p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:16px">Every recommendation explains the problem, the alternatives and the likely consequences.</p></div>
        <div><span class="cell-num">02 · DISCIPLINE</span><h3 style="margin:12px 0 8px">Build what can be run</h3><p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:16px">Reviewed changes, useful documentation, real monitoring and sensible safeguards.</p></div>
        <div><span class="cell-num">03 · HONESTY</span><h3 style="margin:12px 0 8px">Evidence over adjectives</h3><p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:16px">We say what’s been done, what’s still an assumption and what hasn’t been measured.</p></div>
        <div><span class="cell-num">04 · OWNERSHIP</span><h3 style="margin:12px 0 8px">Yours to keep</h3><p style="color:var(--ink-2);font-size:16px">You own the code, the docs and the access. No lock-in, and a proper handover.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="name-title">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The name</p><h2 id="name-title">Why “CAVELDON”?</h2></div>
      <p class="intro">It’s a coined name, chosen to stand for confidence, discipline and lasting progress. The meaning comes from the standards we hold, not from an invented history. The <span class="mono">C—</span> mark is a line drawing, like the diagrams we use to explain systems.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBlock />
</BaseLayout>
